{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649238",
      "title": "Managing State & Using Hooks [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "f57d6767bb92843c25bb2ad70868d775313f561f7ebf8f6ba0f33d8ded59b728",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "So we can't use a regular variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 6,
          "en": "for updating the UI because the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 7.92,
          "en": "doesn't execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "Instead, we need a way of telling React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "that we want to update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "And as mentioned at the end of the previous lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "this can be achieved with another crucial React concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 21.15,
          "en": "called state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.15,
          "end": 25.5,
          "en": "This concept is all about registering variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 29.28,
          "en": "you could say, that are handled by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.28,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "and that are updated with help of a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "that's provided by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 37.62,
          "en": "that will also tell React that data changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.62,
          "end": 41.103,
          "en": "and that will therefore cause React to update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "And these special variables, as you could call them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "are created with help of a special function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 53.043,
          "en": "that must be imported from the React library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "So you must add an import statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 61.12,
          "en": "where you import something between curly braces from react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 66.303,
          "en": "and that something is a function called useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 72,
          "en": "This is a so-called React Hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72,
          "end": 75.63,
          "en": "All these functions that start with use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 79.383,
          "en": "in React projects are React Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.52,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "And the special thing about those React Hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "is that they're technically regular functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 89.969,
          "en": "but they must only be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.969,
          "end": 93.36,
          "en": "inside of React component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.36,
          "end": 96.50999999999999,
          "en": "or inside of other React Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.50999999999999,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "For example, custom React Hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 101.763,
          "en": "which is something you'll learn about later in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.72,
          "end": 105.3,
          "en": "But here we have a React component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.3,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "the App component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.503,
          "en": "and therefore in there we can call useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 115.2,
          "en": "And you must call those Hook functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.2,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "like this directly inside of the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 121.44,
          "en": "not nested inside of some other code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.44,
          "end": 125.37,
          "en": "For example not nested inside of this inner function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.37,
          "end": 128.25,
          "en": "This would not be allowed, you must call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.25,
          "end": 131.403,
          "en": "on the top level of the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.39,
          "end": 136.07999999999998,
          "en": "And these are two important rules of Hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.07999999999998,
          "end": 139.12,
          "en": "you must keep in mind and you must be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 144.21,
          "en": "those React Hook functions must only be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.21,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "inside of component functions or custom Hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "as mentioned, but we'll take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 152.613,
          "en": "at this slightly more advanced feature later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 156.15,
          "en": "And they must be called on the top level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 159.48,
          "en": "so not nested inside of some other inner functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 162.903,
          "en": "some if statement, a loop or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.13,
          "end": 167.19,
          "en": "So that's how you call Hook functions like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.19,
          "end": 170.67000000000002,
          "en": "And you will learn about more built in Hook functions later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.67000000000002,
          "end": 173.7,
          "en": "as well as how to build your own functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 175.92000000000002,
          "en": "But this useState Hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.92000000000002,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "is one of the most important Hooks offered by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 183.54,
          "en": "because that's the Hook that will allow us to manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.54,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "some component specific state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 191.91,
          "en": "which is simply some data stored by React, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.91,
          "end": 196.44,
          "en": "which when changed, will trigger this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.44,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "to which this Hook belongs to re-execute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 203.7,
          "en": "to be reevaluated by React, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.7,
          "end": 206.19,
          "en": "And that's exactly what we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 206.19,
          "end": 209.37,
          "en": "Now useState does accept an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.37,
          "end": 213.99,
          "en": "which is basically the default value you want React to store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.99,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "and you want React to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 218.37,
          "en": "when this component is first rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.37,
          "end": 223.257,
          "en": "And here this could be this Please click a button text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 228.66,
          "en": "though, we'll change this later, but for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.66,
          "end": 230.733,
          "en": "this could be our initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 236.94,
          "en": "And then useState will actually return a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 240.12,
          "en": "which you can store in a variable or constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.12,
          "end": 242.22,
          "en": "it doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.22,
          "end": 245.25,
          "en": "And that value that you will get back here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 245.25,
          "end": 247.83,
          "en": "will actually be an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 247.83,
          "end": 252.83,
          "en": "It will be an array that includes exactly two elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 257.73,
          "en": "and it will always be exactly two elements when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.73,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "you use useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 264,
          "en": "And therefore here we can also use array destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264,
          "end": 266.85,
          "en": "a standard JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 266.85,
          "end": 271.773,
          "en": "to store these two elements in two separate constants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.7,
          "end": 275.19,
          "en": "And you can use any names you want here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 275.19,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "for these two elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 279.453,
          "en": "you're pulling out of that returned array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.59000000000003,
          "end": 285,
          "en": "And here I'll name the first element selectedTopic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "let's say, because with those buttons, when I clicked them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 291.33,
          "en": "I am in the end selecting a topic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 291.33,
          "end": 293.043,
          "en": "about which I wanna learn more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 297.68,
          "en": "And I'll name the second element here setSelectedTopic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 302.88,
          "en": "Now these names here as mentioned are up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 302.88,
          "end": 305.64,
          "en": "but with this way of naming these elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 305.64,
          "end": 308.82,
          "en": "I am following the common naming convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.82,
          "end": 312.363,
          "en": "that you will see in pretty much all React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 317.52,
          "en": "I'm naming the first element here, selectedTopic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 317.52,
          "end": 320.13,
          "en": "because this first element in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 320.13,
          "end": 322.53,
          "en": "which we get back from useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.53,
          "end": 325.86,
          "en": "will be the current data snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 325.86,
          "end": 330.57,
          "en": "for this component execution cycle, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.57,
          "end": 333.3,
          "en": "So when this component function is executed first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 333.3,
          "end": 335.34000000000003,
          "en": "it will be this initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 335.34000000000003,
          "end": 336.933,
          "en": "that's stored in selectedTopic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 338.43,
          "end": 342.51,
          "en": "If it's executed again thereafter, for some reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.51,
          "end": 344.403,
          "en": "it will be the updated value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 345.24,
          "end": 346.68,
          "en": "So this first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 346.68,
          "end": 350.07,
          "en": "will be the actual data we're managing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 350.07,
          "end": 354.45,
          "en": "Now I named this second element setSelectedTopic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 354.45,
          "end": 356.7,
          "en": "because this second element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 356.7,
          "end": 359.4,
          "en": "in this array we get back from useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 359.4,
          "end": 362.553,
          "en": "will always be a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 363.39,
          "end": 366.03,
          "en": "A function provided by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 366.03,
          "end": 370.74,
          "en": "that can be executed to update this state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 370.74,
          "end": 373.503,
          "en": "so to update this stored value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 374.49,
          "end": 378.21,
          "en": "But in a addition to updating this stored value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 378.21,
          "end": 382.5,
          "en": "calling this special function, this second element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 382.5,
          "end": 386.91,
          "en": "will also tell React that this component function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 386.91,
          "end": 389.28,
          "en": "must be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 389.28,
          "end": 392.37,
          "en": "And that's, of course, the important part here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 392.37,
          "end": 395.223,
          "en": "because that's the piece that was missing before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 396.06,
          "end": 400.74,
          "en": "Now with this UseState Hook, we have a way of telling React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 400.74,
          "end": 404.85,
          "en": "that this component function must be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 404.85,
          "end": 407.37,
          "en": "And that's also why we can use const here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 407.37,
          "end": 410.90999999999997,
          "en": "because this constant here selectedTopic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 410.90999999999997,
          "end": 413.01,
          "en": "will be recreated every time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 413.01,
          "end": 415.59000000000003,
          "en": "this component function executes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 415.59000000000003,
          "end": 418.38,
          "en": "so we don't need to use a variable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 418.38,
          "end": 422.13,
          "en": "But behind the scenes React will store and update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 422.13,
          "end": 424.62,
          "en": "the actual value which will then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 424.62,
          "end": 426.9,
          "en": "be passed on to this constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 426.9,
          "end": 429.39300000000003,
          "en": "when this component function executes again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 430.38,
          "end": 433.53,
          "en": "And therefore, now here in handleSelect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 433.53,
          "end": 436.203,
          "en": "we can call setSelectedTopic here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 438.39,
          "end": 441.753,
          "en": "and set this to our selectedButton value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 443.52,
          "end": 448.52,
          "en": "and down there we can now output selectedTopic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 448.65,
          "end": 453.06,
          "en": "So this state snapshot, this first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 453.06,
          "end": 456,
          "en": "we get back from this useState array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 456,
          "end": 459.69,
          "en": "This is what I'm now outputting down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 459.69,
          "end": 461.073,
          "en": "with curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 463.77,
          "end": 467.64,
          "en": "In addition, I'll also console log selectedTopic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 467.64,
          "end": 469.89,
